Third-Party Open Source Notices & License Summary
===============================================================================

ReadySpec is built exclusively on permissive open-source licenses
(MIT / BSD / Apache-2.0) and intentionally excludes GPL/AGPL runtime libraries
(such as ansible-core). Ansible INI/YAML inventory formats are parsed via
ReadySpec's clean-room parser. The Go migration retains the Python prototype
until the new control plane and Web UI pass M3 acceptance.

1. Goss (v0.4.9 — Embedded Unmodified Official Linux Binaries)
   - Project URL: https://github.com/goss-org/goss
   - Copyright: Copyright (c) 2015 Goss Contributors / Ahmed Elsabbahy
   - License: Apache License, Version 2.0 (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0)
    - Usage: Official linux-amd64 and linux-arm64 binaries are embedded in the
      Go executable and verified against pinned SHA-256 values at startup.
      Native SSH delivery and target execution will be implemented in M2.
    - Full license: internal/goss/assets/LICENSE.goss

2. OpenSSH Client (Legacy Architecture Reference; Not a Go Runtime Dependency)
   - Project URL: https://www.openssh.com/
   - License: BSD-style Permissive License
    - Usage: The new Go control plane will use native SSH rather than invoking
      an external OpenSSH client. No OpenSSH executable is bundled.

